Great ideas.  For you to "show" a monster your proof against attack
type, does the test attack have to be done by the monster itself, or
can the monster also observe the results of attacks done by other
monsters, by some line of sight method?  I think the latter would make
for even more interesting fighting.

A further idea is to allow monsters to observe the weapons in use by
(equipped on?) other particular monsters in line of sight, for the
purpose of mounting a variety of attack types on the hero, with or
without regard to effectiveness; and for monsters to learn (or
intrinsically "know") the default attacks and equipment of other
monster types.

This would all help begin to promote within the game the general,
possibly powerful idea of monster grouping properties, because
monsters would behave differently depending on the configuration of
other monsters present, and this would create a large amount of new
strategy choices for the hero to learn - e.g. what's the best way to
respond in a room containing a centaur, a ninja, and a leprechaun,
based on what they're likely to do as a unit, rather than as
independent actors?

